[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two matte ceramic bowls centered in the frame, filled with a thick, vibrant purple mixed-berry smoothie base, captured from a 3/4 overhead angle. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, with the second bowl softly blurred behind it to represent two servings. The smoothie has a remarkably thick, glossy, velvet-like texture, displaying a deep magenta and violet hue from the blended berries. The surface of the smoothie is smooth but shows natural, irregular swirls from the blending process. The bowls are placed on an aged, weathered oak wooden surface with visible grain. Props include a simple wooden spoon resting casually against the edge of the front bowl, a slightly rumpled linen napkin tucked under one side, and a few stray rolled oats and a tiny sprinkle of cinnamon scattered naturally on the table. Lighting is soft, natural, and directional, coming from a window to the left, creating subtle highlights on the surface of the berry mixture. The overall aesthetic is warm, cozy, and lived-in. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures the moment just after preparation, showing slight, authentic imperfections like a tiny, realistic splash mark on the rim of the bowl and a few stray grains on the wood. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image is indistinguishable from a professional food photograph for a high-end cookbook."
  }
]
